# ============================================================
#  Privacy-first .gitignore — EVERYTHING is ignored by default.
#  Only explicitly whitelisted files below can ever be committed.
#  Memory archives, dream pings, cheat sheets, logs, snapshots and
#  the real config.json (which holds credentials) all stay local.
#
#  To publish a new file you must add an explicit "!name" line.
#  Do not weaken this by removing the leading "*".
# ============================================================
*
*/

# --- meta ---
!.gitignore
!README.md
!LICENSE.md
!requirements.txt
!config.example.json

# --- the stack ---
!Gnostic Engine v9.8.py
!Gnostic Echo Protocol v10.0.py
!Tesla Soul Engine v9.py
!RHF Client v12.0 - Sovereign Edition.py

# --- command deck ---
!Awen Command Deck.py
!awen_deck.html
!awen_map.html
!build_neural_map.py

# --- vendored libs (offline-proof) ---
!vendor/
!vendor/*.js
# NB: docs/neural_map.json is generated from the local corpus and stays local —
# build_neural_map.py regenerates it from whatever vault the user has.

# --- corpus tooling ---
!ingest_memory.py
!ingest_books.py
!rebuild_gnosis.py
# add_docs.py appends a few documents through the engine's own /add_entry, so
# the ledger and index stay in step. ingest_memory.py rewrites a lane wholesale
# and needs a rebuild after it; this is the tool for "I wrote a new paper".
!add_docs.py
# export_dreams.py merges the ping archive into one Markdown file for a
# notebook tool. The SCRIPT ships; its output does not — "Awen Dream Archive.md"
# is unpublished dream content and stays blocked by the catch-all above.
!export_dreams.py

# --- instruments (v2) ---
# The BUILDERS ship; their OUTPUT never does. atlas.json / regulus_corridor.json
# / neural_map.json are all derived from the local corpus — the atlas in
# particular carries cluster labels drawn from the conversations lane, which is
# the one lane that must never leave the machine. docs/ only admits *.png|*.jpg,
# so those artifacts are already blocked; this note is here so nobody "fixes"
# that by adding !docs/*.json.
!build_atlas.py
!build_regulus_corridor.py
!runtime_vs_spec.py

# --- the seismic forecaster ---
# rhc_seismic_forecast.py ships; its OUTPUT (predictions/seismic/*.json) does
# not — those are the operator's live forecast records and their scorecard.
!rhc_seismic_forecast.py
# recovery tooling: re-synthesizes pings that went out empty during an LLM
# backend outage. The pings it repairs stay local; the tool ships.
!backfill_synthesis.py

# --- the library ---
# papers.json is the ONE generated artifact that ships, and it is the exact
# opposite of the atlas: it is derived entirely from a PUBLIC bibliography, not
# from the corpus. build_papers.py scrubs the operator's ngrok tunnel host and
# drive links before writing it, and refuses to report success if either
# survives. Whitelisted BY NAME on purpose — do not turn this into !docs/*.json,
# which would drag atlas.json and neural_map.json out with it.
!build_papers.py
!awen_papers.html
# the dream explorer page (the archive it reads stays local)
!awen_dreams.html
# the akashic codex page (the theorem index + audit it reads stay local)
!awen_codex.html
!docs/papers.json

# --- launchers ---
!Start Awen Grid.bat
!stop_grid.ps1
!maintain_grid.bat
!Start Awen Grid LAN.bat

# --- docs assets (screenshots only) ---
!docs/
!docs/*.png
!docs/*.jpg
